#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0898 expect=skipped domain=ADAE
#note "PLAN-join-key-one-side-absent-drop QK8 (owner 2026-10-09): ADAE has no USUBJID, so the template entry's ungated USUBJID key would be on the parent's side only - since REG-Q3 it would leave the key and the join would run on STUDYID + AESEQ across subjects. Requirements.Variables.All gains USUBJID, so the study SKIPS. Measured: the old rule skipped this study too, through the template expander's absent-merge-key guard (TokenExpander.firstAbsentMergeKey) - QK8 states that skip in Requirements, where the gate and its reason are visible."
#library standard=adamig version=1-2
#library standard-domains AE CM MH DM LB VS
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Char
col AETERM  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 1 | HEADACHE
CDISCPILOT01 | 2 | NAUSEA
---

dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1
---
